######## 

$ kagebunshin project init app
created project app with environment dev

-- under a prefix

$ kagebunshin project add-source app dev --provider aws_sm --prefix bin/ --profile acme-dev
added a source to environment dev of project app; it replaces the default source, the local store's section, unless you add `--provider file` too

$ kagebunshin status
daemon: unlocked
providers:
  aws_sm  profile acme-dev  ok
project: app
env: dev
.env.example: none found
1 key
  TEXT  aws_sm:bin/text
warning: aws_sm prefix bin/ (profile acme-dev): skipped secret bin/blob, which is binary

$ kagebunshin run -- sh -c 'echo text is ${TEXT:+set}'
kagebunshin: warning: aws_sm prefix bin/ (profile acme-dev): skipped secret bin/blob, which is binary
kagebunshin: warning: no .env.example found, so every key the environment has is passed (1 key); `kagebunshin project example` writes one from the keys the code reads, to pass only those
text is set

$ kagebunshin list --keys --prefix bin/ --profile acme-dev
2 matches
  bin/blob  aws_sm  (keys not read: secret bin/blob is binary; only string secrets are supported)
  bin/text  aws_sm  TEXT

-- named on its own

$ kagebunshin project add-env app only
added environment only to project app

$ kagebunshin project add-source app only --provider aws_sm --secret bin/blob --key BLOB --profile acme-dev
added a source to environment only of project app; it replaces the default source, the local store's section, unless you add `--provider file` too

$ kagebunshin --env only run -- true
kagebunshin: cannot resolve environment only of project app: aws_sm secret bin/blob (profile acme-dev): secret bin/blob is binary; only string secrets are supported
hint: kagebunshin reads no binary secret: take it out with `kagebunshin project remove-source app only 1`
[exit 1]
